{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they shall take the gold</b> — Behold, all the commands until now were directed at Moses himself: 'And you shall make,' 'you shall make' (Exodus 26:1). And now He commanded that he speak to all the wise of heart, that they should make the garments. Therefore it says <b>and they shall take the gold</b> — that they should receive the donation from the congregation and make the garments from it. And the reason for saying this is that they should neither weigh out the donation for them nor reckon it, for they are trustworthy, as it says (II Kings 12:16): 'And they did not reckon with the men into whose hands they gave the silver to give to the craftsmen, for in faithfulness they deal.' And what is stated regarding the garments — the same rule applies to all the work of the Tabernacle, for only on the first day is it written 'And they took from before Moses' (Exodus 36:3), and even that — they took everything from before him without reckoning, and on the remaining days they brought to them, and therefore it is written (Exodus 36:5), 'And they spoke to Moses, saying: The people are bringing too much.' For to them they would bring, not that they would give it to Moses and he would weigh it out to them; rather, they, after they had gathered everything, counted and weighed and told Moses, as it is written (Exodus 38:24), 'And the gold of the wave offering was,' etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:17:04.290857331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}